do_GET now refuses any request whose Host header is not exactly 127.0.0.1:<bound port> (send_error 403, including a missing Host header); foreign hosts, localhost (DNS rebinding vector), and port mismatches are all rejected. Every response (200/403/404, send_error included) now carries Content-Security-Policy (strict: default/script/style/connect/img 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'), X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff, X-Frame-Options: DENY, Referrer-Policy: no-referrer. The console's inline <style> block moved to an external /console.css route so the strict CSP needs no 'unsafe-inline'. Health-only contract preserved: no compute, idle, pipeline not invoked.

Tests modules/distillery/tests/test_m9_serve_hardening.py: 12 tests (host validation x6 incl. raw-socket missing-Host, security headers x4 incl. 404 + no-inline-style assertion, console contract x2). Fail-before vs shipped serve.py: 9/12 FAIL; pass-after: 12/12 OK; serve.py compiles clean.

